## Hints (ordered)

- Step 2: under-reaction stories put "slow information diffusion" on the
  other side; behavioral stories put "investors selling winners too early".
  Both can't be the whole story — note the tension.
- Q2: a t-stat is (roughly) "how many standard errors the estimate sits from
  zero" — its size is about *evidence strength*, not *money*.
